(NULL, 'mc', 'What is the fastest land animal?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'easy', true, '[{"label":"Lion","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Cheetah","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Horse","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Greyhound","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'The cheetah is the fastest land animal, capable of reaching speeds of up to 112 km/h in short sprints.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'What is the main ingredient in glass?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'easy', true, '[{"label":"Clay","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Sand","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Water","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Salt","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Glass is made primarily from silica sand, which is melted at very high temperatures and then cooled quickly.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'How long does it take for Earth to orbit the Sun once?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'easy', true, '[{"label":"One month","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Six months","isCorrect":false},{"label":"One year","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Two years","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Earth takes approximately 365.25 days — one year — to complete one orbit around the Sun. The extra quarter day is why we have leap years.'),

-- age_band: 7_8 | difficulty: medium
(NULL, 'mc', 'Which animal has the longest lifespan of any vertebrate on Earth?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'medium', true, '[{"label":"Giant tortoise","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Greenland shark","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Bowhead whale","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Koi fish","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'The Greenland shark can live for over 400 years, making it the longest-lived vertebrate animal known to science.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'What is the only mammal that can truly fly?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'medium', true, '[{"label":"Flying squirrel","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Sugar glider","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Bat","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Flying lemur","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Bats are the only mammals capable of true, sustained flight. Other "flying" mammals like sugar gliders can only glide.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'What percentage of the human body is water?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'medium', true, '[{"label":"Around 30%","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Around 45%","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Around 60%","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Around 80%","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'About 60% of the human body is made up of water. It is essential for nearly every function in our bodies.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'What causes thunder during a storm?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'medium', true, '[{"label":"Clouds colliding together","isCorrect":false},{"label":"The rapid expansion of air heated by lightning","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Rain hitting the ground hard","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Wind bouncing between clouds","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Lightning superheats the surrounding air, causing it to rapidly expand and create a shockwave — that''s the sound of thunder.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'What is the name of the force that keeps us on the ground?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'medium', true, '[{"label":"Magnetism","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Friction","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Gravity","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Pressure","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Gravity is the force that attracts objects with mass toward each other. Earth''s gravity keeps us on the ground and the Moon in orbit.'),

