(NULL, 'mc', 'What is the chemical symbol for gold?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'hard', true, '[{"label":"Go","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Gd","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Au","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Gl","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Gold''s chemical symbol is "Au," from the Latin word "aurum," meaning gold. It has been prized by humans for thousands of years.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'Which country has the most wild tigers?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'hard', true, '[{"label":"China","isCorrect":false},{"label":"Russia","isCorrect":false},{"label":"India","isCorrect":true},{"label":"Indonesia","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'India is home to more than 70% of the world''s wild tiger population, thanks in part to its conservation programmes.'),
(NULL, 'mc', 'How long is a light year?', 'fun_facts', '7_8', 'hard', true, '[{"label":"The distance light travels in one hour","isCorrect":false},{"label":"The distance light travels in one year","isCorrect":true},{"label":"One thousand kilometres","isCorrect":false},{"label":"The age of the universe","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'A light year is the distance that light travels in one year — approximately 9.46 trillion kilometres!'),

